---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import ScreenshotFigure from "../components/ScreenshotFigure.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Meeting Pulse works | So the right person knows"
  description="How Meeting Pulse tells the people you live with whether you're in a meeting, without exposing meeting titles or anything else."
  canonicalPath="/how-it-works/"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="How it works"
    title="A short path from your Mac to one quiet answer."
    description="Meeting Pulse has two surfaces on purpose: the Mac app does the watching, and the page your loved one opens does the reading."
  >
    <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg)">
      <a class="button button--accent" href="/download/">Start with the Mac app</a>
      <a class="button" href="/privacy/">What stays private</a>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="workflow">
      <article class="workflow-step">
        <span class="workflow-step__index">01</span>
        <div class="workflow-step__copy">
          <h3>Install Station</h3>
          <p>
            The owner installs the native macOS app and grants the Accessibility
            permission needed for supported detection.
          </p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/install-macos/">Install guide</a>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step__visual">
          <ScreenshotFigure
            light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-onboarding-window-light.jpg"
            dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-onboarding-window-dark.jpg"
            alt="Meeting Pulse onboarding window on macOS"
            caption="Setup starts in Station."
            width={1120}
            height={400}
          />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="workflow-step">
        <span class="workflow-step__index">02</span>
        <div class="workflow-step__copy">
          <h3>Watch a supported meeting state</h3>
          <p>
            Station observes the supported call surfaces locally. It does not
            upload meeting content or turn the browser into a sensor.
          </p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/accessibility-permission/">Why Accessibility?</a>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step__visual">
          <ScreenshotFigure
            light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-watch-available-light.jpg"
            dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-watch-available-dark.jpg"
            alt="Meeting Pulse Station showing an available state"
            caption="The owner can see what the detector knows."
          />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="workflow-step">
        <span class="workflow-step__index">03</span>
        <div class="workflow-step__copy">
          <h3>Pair the person who needs to know</h3>
          <p>
            Station creates a private viewer path. The person checking in opens
            that link on a phone or laptop without creating an account.
          </p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/pairing/">Pair a viewer</a>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step__visual">
          <ScreenshotFigure
            light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-sharing-viewers-light.jpg"
            dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-sharing-viewers-dark.jpg"
            alt="Meeting Pulse Station showing paired viewers"
            caption="The owner chooses who gets the link."
          />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="workflow-step">
        <span class="workflow-step__index">04</span>
        <div class="workflow-step__copy">
          <h3>Read the state, not the story</h3>
          <p>
            The viewer checks the current signal periodically. If the signal is
            stale or unavailable, the viewer says so instead of guessing.
          </p>
          <a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Troubleshooting states</a>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step__visual">
          <ScreenshotFigure
            light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-viewer-status-unavailable-light.jpg"
            dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-viewer-status-unavailable-dark.jpg"
            alt="Meeting Pulse viewer showing unavailable meeting status"
            caption="“Meeting status unavailable” is an honest answer."
            width={1280}
            height={577}
          />
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Meeting Pulse is not a realtime presence system.</strong>
      <p>
        The owner heartbeat and viewer polling are periodic. That is why
        freshness and unavailable states are part of the product language.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
